      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults under medical supervision (3,200 mg/day). The usual single dose is 400\u2013800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It may be a typo, for example 1600 mg total per day or 400 mg four times daily.\n\n2. **You said you're not a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, who can confirm the indication and the patient's details.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose or enter the order directly. If they give me a corrected, clinician-verified order, such as ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, I can enter it."
      }
