       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose. You're not a prescriber, so your confirmation isn't a clinical verification of it.\n- **I can't verify that a prescriber approved it.** If a clinician really intends this dose, they should enter it themselves or contact pharmacy. Either route has safety checks that I'm not able to replace.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Ask the prescriber to review the order. It may be a mistake.\n- If they want a standard dose, I can enter it once they confirm it. Examples are 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, within 3,200 mg/day.\n- If the patient needs pain or inflammation control urgently, the care team can reach the on-call physician or pharmacist right away."
